# The route's next hop is fd00::2 and the peer is fd00::3, and they must differ.
# RFC 4271 Section 5.1.3 forbids advertising a peer its own address as NEXT_HOP,
# and originatedNextHopIsPeerOwn (forward_next_hop.go) withholds such a route.
# Explicit setup assigns fd00::2/128, fd00::3/127 and fe80::1/128 to loopback.
# ONE connected prefix, fd00::2/127, contains speaker, next-hop owner and peer;
# fe80::1 belongs to the same next-hop owner. The Next Hop field is 32 octets.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-1 positive -- the Next Hop field carries the global IPv6
# address first and the link-local address second. The asserted MP_REACH_NLRI is 800E36
# 0002 01 20, then FD000000000000000000000000000002 (fd00::2, the route's next hop), then
# FE800000000000000000000000000001 (fe80::1, the next-hop owner's link-local). Order is
# pinned by offset, so a swapped pair fails.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-2 positive -- the Length of Next Hop Network Address octet is
# 0x20 (32) because a link-local address is also included in the Next Hop field.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-3 positive -- one connected prefix fd00::2/127 contains the
# speaker and global next hop fd00::2 and recipient fd00::3. ze evaluates that condition
# against the host interface table; the `local-link-local fe80::1` leaf supplies the
# next-hop owner's assigned address, it does not decide inclusion.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-4 negative -- the "in all other cases" branch does not fire
# while the inclusion condition holds. The field is not reduced to the global address
# alone, and the length octet is not 16.
#
# Pairs with conf-llnh-lla-only.ci, which carries the SAME `local-link-local fe80::1` leaf
# and the same capability, and differs in one variable only: its route's next hop sits on
# no locally connected subnet.
option=file:conf-llnh-update.conf
option=bind:ipv6
1:cmd:announce ipv6 unicast 2001:db8:1::1/128 next-hop fd00::2 origin igp local-preference 100
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:005E02:000000474001010040020040050400000064800E3600020120FD000000000000000000000000000002FE800000000000000000000000000001008020010DB8000100000000000000000001
1:cmd:announce eor ipv6 unicast
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:001E02:00000007900F0003000201
